Sources</button></div><div class="md:flex md:flex-wrap md:space-y-0 relative mb-4 text-gray-800 md:mb-6 md:px-8 md:before:inset-x-8"><div class="typo-timestamp text-xs text-gray-600"><span data-testid="article-published-time">Published <!-- -->Wed, Mar 23, 2016 · 09:50 PM</span></div></div><div class="paywall-content typo-article-body mx-auto my-4 text-gray-800 md:px-8 group-data-[language=ms]:font-poppins group-data-[language=ta]:font-notoSansTamil mb-4 md:mb-6 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:relative [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:after:absolute [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:after:inset-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:after:bg-gradient-to-t [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:after:from-white [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:after:to-transparent" data-testid="article-body-container"><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words mb-4 md:mb-6" data-testid="article-paragraph-component">Singapore</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words mb-4 md:mb-6" data-testid="article-paragraph-component">THE e-commerce game is strong in Singapore. Homegrown platforms ezbuy (known formerly as 65daigou and which provides Taobao shopping services) and iFashion (a new roll-up play which targets online fashion sites) have raised US$20 million and S$1 million respectively in venture capital, amid a competitive landscape.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words mb-4 md:mb-6" data-testid="article-paragraph-component">On Wednesday, ezbuy - an aggregator shopping site that connects Singapore customers directly to overseas online merchants from Taobao (China), the US and Taiwan - announced its Series B round led by Vision Knight Capital and joined by existing investors IDG Ventures and CGC Capital.</p></div><div data-testid="article-tags-component" class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mb-8 mt-11 md:px-8 lg:-mx-6"><a class="!text-gray-800 hover:text-gray-800 hover:underline hover:underline-offset-4 tracking-2 whitespace-normal break-all rounded-full bg-gray-200 p-3 font-poppins text-2xs font-semibold leading-150 tracking-2 text-gray-800 !no-un